Problem: During the World Cup, there are \( n \) different Panini stickers to collect. Marco's friends are trying to complete their collection, but nobody has a full set of stickers yet! A pair of his friends are said to be wholesome if their combined collection has at least one of each sticker. Marco knows the contents of everyone's collections, and wants to take them all to a restaurant for his birthday. However, he doesn't want any wholesome pairs sitting at the same table.

(i) Show that Marco might need to reserve at least \( n \) different tables.

(ii) Show that \( n \) tables will always be enough for Marco to achieve his goal.

Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.<|im_end|>
<|im_start|>assistant


Completion:
### Solution:

#### Part (i): Show that Marco might need to reserve at least \( n \) different tables

1. Consider a scenario where there are exactly 2 people with the same collection each person is unique to their combination of stickers so there's one sticker that no one else in the collection group has which is their specific one.
    - If Marco has \( n \) different combinations then at least \( \lceil n \rceil \geq n+1) >\) need for additional seats for each individual having this one special individual person without duplication.

Thus it shows why needing \( n \) unique tables would guarantee uniqueness among these different sets/groups being able to sit comfortably at different places without overlapping anyone who already shared with anyone else.

Thus showing how much table needs to reserve for uniqueness among these combinations of individual unique groups.

2 To show why needing only n people then they should reserve enough tables so they can fit everyone comfortably without overlap meaning if each one sitting alone doesn't matter anymore but still ensuring enough separate areas where everyone can find their seat individually without having someone share with same individual sitting alone together separately meaning showing how much tables required showing minimum requirement needed.


Thus \( \boxed{n}\leq n tables needed .<|endoftext|>
